# per-word timing sidecars: ROLLED OUT 2026-09-17. 1,901 files, 68 MB,
# tracked and published -- they are what makes word-level click-to-seek and
# highlighting work. Pages without one fall back to sentence-level seek via
# the data-t attribute, which is what the site did before and after.

# alignment resume checkpoint: transient, deleted once model.pkl is written
aligned.checkpoint.pkl
*.checkpoint.pkl

# Speaker voice embeddings -- BIOMETRIC DATA, must never be published.
# These are pyannote voiceprints for everyone who spoke at a public meeting,
# including private residents giving public comment. A transcript records what
# someone said in public (the point of this project, and the city publishes the
# video); a voiceprint is a biometric index that supports identifying them
# against unrelated audio. Nobody speaking at a council meeting expects that.
# They were served at https://<site>/<dir>/embeddings.pkl with HTTP 200 until
# 2026-09-17. Keep them locally -- cross-video speaker matching needs them and
# they are expensive to rebuild -- but never in a published tree.
embeddings.pkl

# Auto-accept whitelist: holds contributor bearer tokens, and this repo is
# public. Committing it would publish the exact value that grants the
# privilege. trusted_contributors.example.json is the tracked template.
trusted_contributors.json

# Correction queue: contains submitted free text from the public, pending
# review. Keep triage local until a submission has actually been reviewed.
corrections_queue.json

